# Statements the transparent cache is allowed to serve.
#
# It starts EMPTY, on purpose. That is the whole demo: bring everything up,
# watch the client report which queries are slow, add those queries here, and
# run `barnacle reload-config`. Nothing restarts, and the client gets faster
# without noticing that anything happened.
#
# Matching is an exact byte match against the statement text on the wire -- no
# normalisation, no parameter extraction. A statement that differs by one
# space is a different statement, which is why the five below are copied in
# rather than retyped.
#
# Add them from inside the controller, so the daemon reads the same filesystem
# you wrote to:
#
#   docker compose -f demo/docker-compose.yml exec ctl sh -c \
#       'cat demo/config/slow-queries.list >> demo/config/cache.list'
#   docker compose -f demo/docker-compose.yml exec ctl barnacle reload-config
#
# To start over, empty it again and reload.
# The five slow statements, ready to paste into cache.list.
#
# This is the ANSWER, kept beside the demo so you do not have to transcribe it
# from the client's log. In a real deployment you would arrive at this list by
# reading the log yourself: the client reports every query over 500ms, and
# these are the five that show up.
#
#   cat demo/config/slow-queries.list >> demo/config/cache.list
#   barnacle reload-config

SELECT * FROM inventory_report WHERE category = 'safety'
SELECT * FROM order_history WHERE status = 'shipped'
SELECT * FROM brand_rollup
SELECT * FROM customer_spend
SELECT * FROM category_margin
